# daemon/sum_core.c builds it over channels/; <name>.prompt, the templated
# prompt's token ids, one a line; <name>.steps, a line a step of the answer:
# the token taken, the step's largest logit's token, and its margin over the
# second (the logits before the grammar); <name>.logits0.f32, the first step's
# logits, float32 little-endian. tokens.txt: a text's ids, a tab, the text (\n,
# \t, \\ escaped). kl.txt, kl.ids: the held-out text and its tokens.
# <name> <prompt tokens> <answer steps>, then kl_tokens, kl_chunk, and
# kl_unsloth_q4_k_m, the KL divergence of the file the previous engine ran,
